-- mlir_pass.mm0 — PC09's pass-boundary obligations, stated and cited.
--
-- PC09 asks for captured pre/post IR for every selected pass of
-- `Austral → KernelIR → MLIR → device IR` *and* a relation at each boundary.
-- The captures exist: `mm0/proof_chain/mlir/stage.toml` records seventeen
-- captured rows — the two head passes, the lowering segment's fourteen passes
-- *individually* (each from the pipeline's own `--mlir-print-ir-after-all`
-- dump), and the conversion — plus one uncaptured row, `nvvm-to-ptx`, on
-- purpose. What this file adds is the other half — one named obligation per
-- captured row, so "capture is not preservation" stops being a sentence and
-- becomes a list of statements that a proof could later discharge, or that a
-- reviewer can reject one at a time.
--
-- There is still no MLIR semantics in this repository: no dialect has an
-- interpretation here, so the relations below are *uninterpreted* and nothing
-- in this file says any of them holds. `scripts/mlir-chain claims` is what this
-- file is checked against, and it only checks shape and freshness:
--
--   * every captured pass row of `stage.toml` has exactly one obligation here,
--     and no obligation names a pass the record does not capture — so a new
--     capture cannot arrive without its statement, and a statement cannot
--     outlive its capture;
--   * each obligation's `pre=` / `post=` are the record's own `pre_file` /
--     `post_file` for that pass, so the endpoints are the bytes the record
--     hashes, not a paraphrase;
--   * every `-- cites:` digest is the current content of the file it names, so
--     a changed MLIR endpoint or record fails this file rather than silently
--     leaving it describing the previous route;
--   * the file carries no `axiom` and no `theorem` (checked by both this
--     script and `scripts/verify-invariants`), because a stated obligation is
--     not an admitted one.
--
-- The intended meaning, written here where a reviewer can disagree with it:
-- for a boundary `p` with pre module `a` and post module `b`,
--
--     p_preserves a b    means    ∀ i v,  denotes a i v  ↔  denotes b i v
--
-- i.e. the post module computes exactly the values the pre module computed, at
-- every observation index. That is the relation each pass of this route has to
-- satisfy; it is deliberately *strong* (it forbids a pass that merely refines
-- definedness, for instance). The equivalences themselves are not stated: MM0
-- has no built-in equality and defining one would import a theory this artifact
-- has not earned, exactly as in `mm0/store_projection.mm0`. What is pinned here
-- is which pair of files each claim is about.
--
-- What this file is NOT:
--   * not a certificate — see "no axiom, no theorem" above;
--   * not a statement about *whether* a pass changed the IR: several of the
--     fourteen after-dumps are byte-identical to the one before them (the five
--     cited at seg08…seg13 among them), so their obligations are reflexive on
--     this module — an observation about `clamp`, not a proof of the pass;
--   * not a statement about the five uncaptured passes after the conversion, or
--     about the PTX they produce (G19a pins that PTX; PC10 owns instructions);
--   * not a refinement of *any* other layer: it says nothing about KernelIR
--     (`mm0/` PC04), the WGSL path (PC05), or the device.
--
-- The `[gap]` is the honest state: four obligations are written down, cited and
-- bound to the current captures, and none is proved. Discharging them needs a
-- semantics for the `gpu`/`nvvm`/`arith`/`cf` dialects in a prover this repo
-- can replay (the Lean side of `mm0/toy_witness/` is the shape that would take),
-- which does not exist yet.
--
-- Citations are by content, so a digest here means "this claim is about these
-- bytes": the record, and each module that appears as a boundary endpoint.
-- cites: mm0/proof_chain/mlir/stage.toml sha256=d83556276f9a4f6b6347873d03931fd74697091a02398cab6aa33b1e23452c15
-- cites: mm0/proof_chain/mlir/ir/clamp.kernelir sha256=52d01cfaade3df43f28ad9e017b07b97d123f498563fb3a22c0cc075864db5a5
-- cites: mm0/proof_chain/mlir/ir/clamp.mlir sha256=e17b0a0b6b4ab20dc8d0be93c58fb51f9e7c0535ba3c93961381c1bab1abbd58
-- cites: mm0/proof_chain/mlir/ir/clamp.canonical.mlir sha256=5acf98dc750edcb131ed4aacadfdabc31c69948c0c5992e93518f4e2cb8c19c8
-- cites: mm0/proof_chain/mlir/ir/clamp.seg01.mlir sha256=7534017e7d10d257305b2450e4617ca866ba51b7eed6e6086ec60f9bd6d3ef89
-- cites: mm0/proof_chain/mlir/ir/clamp.seg02.mlir sha256=7534017e7d10d257305b2450e4617ca866ba51b7eed6e6086ec60f9bd6d3ef89
